# Cursor Editor — Context Windows & Compaction

## Overview

Cursor's AI agents operate within constrained context windows — finite token limits that determine how much conversation history and code context the agent can process at once. Understanding how context windows work and how Cursor handles compaction (summarizing older content) is essential for maintaining effective agent interactions during long sessions.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[New conversation starts] --> B[Fresh context window]
    B --> C[Agent processes prompt]
    C --> D[Conversation grows]
    D --> E{Context window near limit?}
    E -->|No| F[Continue adding messages]
    F --> D
    E -->|Yes| G[Compaction triggered]
    G --> H[Summarize older messages]
    H --> I[Create compacted context]
    I --> J[Agent continues with summary]
    J --> K{New @-references added?}
    K -->|Yes| L[Explicit context preserved]
    K -->|No| M[Only summary available]
    L --> N[Agent has fresh + summary]
    M --> N
    N --> O[Continue conversation]
```

---

## Context Window Mechanics

### What Gets Included in Context

| Content Source | Inclusion Priority | Behavior |
|---------------|-------------------|----------|
| **Recent messages** | Highest | Always included |
| **Current file** | High | Auto-included when agent reads/edits |
| **@-references** | Highest | Always preserved, explicit inclusion |
| **Open editor tabs** | Medium | Recently active tabs included |
| **Older messages** | Lowest | Compact when window fills |
| **Rule files** | High | Loaded based on matching globs |
| **Skill files** | High | Loaded when triggered |

### Context Window Sizes

| Setting | Minimum | Default | Maximum | Use Case |
|---------|---------|---------|---------|----------|
| `cursor.agent.contextWindow` | 4,000 | 128,000 | 200,000 | Full conversation |
| `cursor.agent.tabContextWindow` | 1,000 | 8,192 | 16,384 | Tab completions only |

### Token Budget Allocation

The context window is shared across all sources:

```
Total context window: 128,000 tokens
  - System prompt: ~500 tokens (fixed)
  - Rules: ~2,000 tokens (varies)
  - Conversation history: ~80,000 tokens (dynamic)
  - @-references: ~20,000 tokens (dynamic)
  - Current file: ~10,000 tokens (dynamic)
  - Buffer/reserve: ~15,500 tokens
```

### Recency Bias

Cursor exhibits recency bias — newer messages are more likely to be retained than older ones:

| Position | Retention Likelihood | Notes |
|----------|---------------------|-------|
| **Last 5 messages** | ~100% | Always retained |
| **Messages 6-20** | ~80% | High retention, compacted last |
| **Messages 21-50** | ~50% | Partially summarized |
| **Messages 50+** | ~20% | Fully summarized or removed |

