## Compaction Flow Details

### How Compaction Works Step by Step

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant A as Agent
    participant S as System
    participant M as Model
    
    U->>A: Send message (context 85% full)
    A->>S: Check context size
    S-->>A: 108,800 / 128,000 tokens
    A->>M: Request response
    M->>A: Response starts...
    Note over S: Context reaches 95%
    S->>S: Trigger compaction
    S->>S: Identify @-references to preserve
    S->>S: Summarize older messages
    S->>S: Create compacted context
    S->>A: Notify compaction complete
    A->>U: Continue with summary context
```

### Compaction Summary Example

Before compaction (120K tokens):
```
Message 1: "Set up Express server with TypeScript" [Agent: full code]
Message 2: "Add user routes" [Agent: full code]
Message 3: "Add authentication" [Agent: full code]
Message 4: "Add rate limiting" [Agent: full code]
Message 5: "Add error handling" [Agent: full code]
Message 6: Current conversation...
Message 7: Latest messages (preserved)
```

After compaction (45K tokens):
```
[Summary of earlier messages]
- Project: Express + TypeScript server
- Features added: user routes, auth, rate limiting, error handling
- Key decisions: JWT auth, express-rate-limit, custom error middleware

[Preserved content]
Message 6: Current conversation...
Message 7: Latest messages
Message 8: @file server.ts (preserved verbatim)
```

