## Relationship to @-References

### How @-References Survive Compaction

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[User adds @-reference] --> B{@-reference type?}
    B -->|@file path| C[Add full file to context]
    B -->|@folder path/| D[Add folder files to context]
    B -->|@code symbol| E[Add symbol to context]
    
    C --> F[Context added to window]
    D --> F
    E --> F
    
    F --> G{Compaction triggered?}
    G -->|Yes| H[@-references preserved]
    G -->|No| I[Continue normally]
    
    H --> J[Agent has @-referenced content]
    I --> J
```

### @-Reference Priority During Compaction

| Priority | Content | Compaction Behavior |
|----------|---------|---------------------|
| **1 (Highest)** | `@code` specific symbols | Always preserved |
| **2** | `@file` files under 50 lines | Always preserved |
| **3** | `@folder` directories | Always preserved |
| **4** | Recent conversation | Preserved if within window |
| **5** | Older conversation | Summarized/compacted |
| **6** | Oldest conversation | Removed first |

