## Context Window Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Agent forgets earlier instructions | Compaction removed context | Use @-references to preserve |
| Agent repeats work already done | Summary didn't capture decisions | Ask agent to recap before continuing |
| Long responses truncated | `maxTokens` too low | Increase `cursor.agent.maxTokens` |
| Slow responses with large context | Window near max | Start fresh session, use task segmentation |
| @-references not working | File too large for window | Use `@code` instead of `@file` |

### Diagnostic Commands

```bash
# Check current context window usage
claude --env

# Test with smaller context to force compaction
claude --context-window 8192 "Test agent with limited context"

# Verify @-reference survival
claude --output json "Can you see the code I referenced with @code?"

# Check compaction logs
# In Agent Output channel, search for "compaction" or "summarize"
```

